From 3bbfd8b25adc15a01140070ca16e26426ff8cec9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] fix(frontend): SSE reader delivers the last line and
 cancels on exit; memoised Markdown; stable message keys; local calendar days
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F-4: the inline SSE loop in ChatPanel processed only complete lines, so a
final `data:` event without a trailing newline (the tail of a stream or a
reply cut short by the server) was silently dropped; `data:` without a
space (legal SSE, emitted by some proxies) was ignored; and the reader was
never cancelled when the loop exited early, leaving the connection open
after Stop or an error. lib/sse.ts (readSseEvents, splitSseLines,
parseSseDataLine) fixes all three, handles CRLF and UTF-8 split across
chunks, and is unit-tested; ChatPanel iterates it.

F-5: MarkdownContent rebuilt its `components` and `remarkPlugins` objects on
every render and was not memoised, so every streamed token re-created the
Markdown tree of every finished message. Tables are module-level and the
export is React.memo. Message rows were keyed by index, so deleting or
inserting a message re-mounted every row below it; stableMessageKeys()
derives unique keys from clientMessageId/id + role + model with an index
fallback, never duplicates.

F-8: Reports date presets and the chat-export filename used
toISOString().slice(0, 10) — the UTC day — and were a day off for users
east of Greenwich in the evening; both use localDateKey now.

Tests: lib/sse.test.ts, lib/messageKeys.test.ts, memo assertion in
MarkdownContent.test.tsx. vitest 41 files / 224 tests; tsc clean; build ok.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
